#NEXUS

[ lü2004a_fig8: Slanted cladogram with every branch a straight diagonal from its node (classed slanted, no spine): check against the out-of-scope ruling for slanted diagrams. Allosauroidea and Ornithomimidae both leave the root point, so the root is a polytomy of three. Several branches leave from part way along other branches rather than from a fork (Chirostenotes and the large oviraptorid clade from the Khaan line). 20 tips, 1 polytomies (3 children). Sample 10 case (census 3, seed 20261274). Topology transcribed from the figure image and checked node by node; topology only. ]

BEGIN TAXA;
    DIMENSIONS NTAX=20;
    TAXLABELS
        Allosauroidea
        Ornithomimidae
        Dromaeosauridae
        Troodontidae
        Archaeopteryx_lithographica
        Incisivosaurus_gauthieri
        Caudipteryx_zoui
        Microvenator_celer
        Avimimus_portentosus
        Chirostenotes_pergracilis
        Khaan_mckennai
        Nomingia_gobiensis
        Oviraptor_mongoliensis
        Ingenia_yanshini
        Conchoraptor_gracilis
        Heyuannia_huangi
        Nemegtia_barsboldi
        Citipati_osmolskae
        GIN_100/42
        Oviraptor_philoceratops
    ;
END;

BEGIN TREES;
    TREE lü2004a_fig8 = [&R] (Allosauroidea,Ornithomimidae,(Dromaeosauridae,((Troodontidae,Archaeopteryx_lithographica),(Incisivosaurus_gauthieri,(Caudipteryx_zoui,(Microvenator_celer,(Avimimus_portentosus,(Chirostenotes_pergracilis,(Khaan_mckennai,(((((Nomingia_gobiensis,Oviraptor_mongoliensis),Ingenia_yanshini),Conchoraptor_gracilis),(Heyuannia_huangi,(Nemegtia_barsboldi,Citipati_osmolskae))),(GIN_100/42,Oviraptor_philoceratops)))))))))));
END;
